{"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Sample Writing answers","y":0.14043826732945641,"x":0.083996268925138937,"h":0.035582826612133189,"c":1,"w":0.47190800984700526},{"x":0.16218684035918698,"h":0.01866578887292436,"t":"Additional sample Writing answers","y":0.20210087911075636,"w":0.27023386637369795,"c":1},{"y":0.22048424088232277,"h":0.014588089798027615,"t":"in Resource bank","w":0.1424651845296224,"x":0.16024052313382417,"c":1},{"h":0.020360820846647476,"x":0.084362135101337027,"y":0.27179034211050124,"w":0.33539095560709631,"t":"TEST 1, WRITING TASK 1","c":1},{"y":0.30655243655707154,"w":0.65240870157877606,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.0 score.","x":0.084286780985502546,"h":0.018700333450371254,"c":1},{"h":0.017667844522968101,"c":1,"t":"The table depicts the outcomes of a questionare of how often people buy and drink a different types","x":0.084362139174021036,"y":0.33274440521915682,"w":0.78189300537109374},{"x":0.084362133834327432,"t":"of coffee in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Adelaide, and Hobart of Australia.","y":0.3517441858594974,"w":0.59465021769205728,"h":0.020458405655320644,"c":1},{"x":0.084290407517093519,"y":0.37781641680236699,"t":"The first option is bought fresh coffee in last 4 weeks. In Sydney has 43.7 per cent of city residents","w":0.77173126220703125,"h":0.020240947691936517,"c":1},{"y":0.39674251411422568,"x":0.084305830764828796,"w":0.78200332641601578,"c":1,"t":"and has almost the same amount as Melbourne which is 42.2 per cent. Brisbane and Adelaide have","h":0.019570713470063561},{"w":0.68930043538411456,"h":0.018950132093665362,"c":1,"t":"a nearly same amount, 34.2 per cent and 34.4 per cent. Next, Hobart has 38.3 per cent.","x":0.084362127792550728,"y":0.41715116317640866},{"w":0.74074076334635419,"h":0.019140164899882128,"y":0.44316843373204562,"x":0.084362128416126156,"c":1,"t":"The second line is bought instant coffee in last 4 weeks. Brisbane has 52.6 per cent. Other two"},{"y":0.46366279053824444,"w":0.77777776082356787,"t":"cities that have amost the same number are Adelaide, 49.8 per cent, and Melbourne, 48.3 per cent.","x":0.084362148277948468,"h":0.017491508569256853,"c":1},{"w":0.76337448120117191,"h":0.018914180032215566,"c":1,"y":0.48255813992399899,"t":"The lowest number is 45.5 per cent of Sydney and The highest number is 54.I per cent of Hobart.","x":0.084362142005743976},{"x":0.084302771901544324,"t":"The last option of the survey shows the percentage of city residents that went to a cafe for coffee","h":0.021436476735540833,"y":0.50706120190051096,"w":0.76143864949544271,"c":1},{"w":0.77983540852864586,"t":"or tea in last 4 weeks. In Sydney, people went to a café for coffee or tea in last 4 weeks 61 per cent","x":0.084362130948861511,"y":0.52761627945563372,"h":0.018909044344377457,"c":1},{"y":0.54561274781042779,"c":1,"t":"of city residents. In Brisbane, citizens went to a café' for coffee of tea in last 4 weeks 55.4 per cent.","w":0.77997090657552071,"h":0.021404218055895874,"x":0.084299145490521615},{"h":0.021585079188622069,"y":0.56538191628064727,"t":"The lowest is Adelaide that shows 49.9 per cent of city residents. In Hobart, people went to a café'","x":0.084309175210028398,"c":1,"w":0.76145126342773439},{"x":0.082190724510556284,"w":0.7697667439778646,"c":1,"t":"for coffee of tea in last 4 weeks 62.7 per cent. The highest is Melbourne that shows 63.3 per cent.","y":0.58500167841623496,"h":0.021472099672638745},{"w":0.75925923665364581,"c":1,"t":"In conclusion, the highest number of the survey is the percentage of city residents that went to a","x":0.082304537924219781,"y":0.6133686690716792,"h":0.017445284570484998},{"x":0.084362127560725267,"c":1,"h":0.018948420197719362,"t":"cafe for coffee or tea in last 4 weeks because it shows almost the highest percentage in 3 types.","w":0.74691360473632817,"y":0.63221437010513826},{"x":0.084231185833589184,"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","w":0.29450668334960939,"h":0.015557573316234863,"y":0.66562239147015656,"c":1},{"x":0.12751182445998638,"h":0.016948412388598344,"c":1,"y":0.69906124701528449,"w":0.7058655802408853,"t":"This answer covers all three categories and shows a good level of grouping and"},{"y":0.71643109530962512,"w":0.69135803222656245,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"x":0.12962962569681755,"t":"comparison of information in each category. The descriptions are supported by"},{"w":0.69357945760091144,"h":0.018791332963779439,"x":0.12748648843860469,"t":"accurate data. Organisation is clear (introduction and overview, one paragraph","y":0.73169305290007669,"c":1},{"x":0.127572021720464,"t":"per category) and there is evidence of cohesive devices [The first option | The","y":0.74999999986648935,"w":0.68724278767903646,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"second line | The last option]. Vocabulary is generally adequate and appropriate","x":0.12748615477767128,"w":0.70591949462890624,"h":0.021027321248228703,"y":0.76528413677732343},{"c":1,"y":0.78343023242534837,"t":"for the task, in spite of occasional errors [questionare \/ questionnaire | amost \/","x":0.12757200442759228,"w":0.68930043538411456,"h":0.014567411690072807},{"c":1,"y":0.80087209289047112,"h":0.014534883982160851,"t":"almostj. Grammar shows a mix of simple and complex sentence structures with","x":0.12757201981258134,"w":0.69958847045898431},{"c":1,"w":0.70370371500651041,"x":0.12757201071911395,"y":0.81684334488699528,"t":"a reasonable level of accuracy. A wider range of vocabulary and\/or grammatical","h":0.016005492463128657},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.83421672559280546,"t":"range would help to improve the score here.","x":0.12551440195749383,"w":0.39711934407552085,"c":1},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"y":0.91860465100676214,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"127","x":0.83127572055230148}],"h":3395}